  "description": "Fuaran.Compute.LinearAlgebra — a small, dense, column-major linear-algebra contract whose every operation runs in one pinned floating-point order, so its answers are byte-identical on .NET, under Fable and in every host that ports it: an opaque immutable Matrix, vectors as Fuaran.Core's Vector<float> (a float column is an input without a copy), the level-1 operations (dot, axpy, scale, add, sub and the scaled norm2), gemv in column-axpy order, gemm in per-element k order, the Gram matrix, triangular solves over a checked UpperTriangular, the one Givens rotation, batch and pivoted Householder factorizations with one rank rule, the bit-pattern wire form of a matrix, typed errors and canonical NaN out. Matrix operations only: regression modelling over them is Fuaran.Compute.Regression. No fused multiply-add and no host mathematics call on any host. Fable-clean.",
